vireshk/vhost abf24853: Generic::reset() and VirtioCommon::reset() return the interrupt
without unwrapping it. Applied after vireshk-vhost-abf24853.patch.

`interrupt_cb` is set only in activate(), when the guest has written DRIVER_OK. reset()
returned `Some(self.interrupt_cb.take().unwrap())`, which panics for a device that was
never activated (a guest created with `xl create -p` and destroyed before it ran, or one
that died before probing the device). In xen-vhost-frontend that panic happens inside
XenDevice::exit() with the FrontendGuests lock held, so the lock is poisoned and the
ioreq server and foreign mappings of the guest are never released: the domain stays
`(null) --p--d`. The field is already an Option, so `take()` is the return value.

Upstream: not opened (draft in xaloqi-knowledge campaigns/2026-11-10-xvf-teardown-issue-draft.md,
issue A); target vireshk/vhost, branch frontend/stable.

